## Statements for OSS-Fuzz fuzz targets
This repository also states theorems about many OSS-Fuzz fuzz targets, proved or not. For each of the $n_oss_fuzz_projects projects in OSS-Fuzz there is a directory under [projects/](projects/).$not_in_oss_fuzz We can build the fuzz targets of $n_oss_fuzz_available of these projects. $n_oss_fuzz_included of their $n_oss_fuzz_targets fuzz targets have statements in this release; [index/STATUS.md](index/STATUS.md) says why the others do not. Each of these fuzz targets is compiled up to four ways ($four_builds), and each build gets Rocq statements about those exact bytes. These are statements, not results: $proved_words

In this release: $status_counts. [analyses/known-issues.md](analyses/known-issues.md) lists every statement that is not open or proved, with the reason.

There are four kinds of statement: a build halts; a sanitizer build agrees with the plain build; the two builds disagree on at most a fraction *b* of a stated input distribution; and the inputs on which they agree are decidable ([docs/statements.md](docs/statements.md)). One example:

